Sval: hooks for the History sidebar and for history clears

Sval's History sidebar lists one workspace's history, has an archived view
that runs no Places query, and fills a device and a workspace column and a
site folder's icon, which PlacesTreeView has no cells for. searchHistory
asks the tree's svalHistory before and after it loads a query, and
PlacesTreeView's getCellText and getImageSrc ask it for a cell first;
SvalHistorySidebar gives the History sidebar's tree that object, and every
other Places tree has none.

Every history clear (Clear Recent History, clearing on shutdown, a policy)
reaches the synced history with the scope the clear dialog chose, so the
Sanitizer's history item runs its clear through SvalHistorySync.

No chrome API changes a sidebar's query, a PlacesTreeView's cells, or what a
history clear does.

